uxury Texas ranch listings frequently spread online because they combine real estate, history and landscapes on a scale most buyers never encounter. The Roosevelt name adds another layer, but the price also reflects the market for large, improved tracts within driving distance of the Dallas-Fort Worth metro area."]}, {"heading": "What comes next", "paragraphs": ["One listing does not define the broader ranch market, but the $21.5 million asking price shows the premium attached to privacy, contiguous acreage, recreational features and metro access. If the property sells near that level, it will become another high-profile example of the value placed on legacy ranch holdings near growing Texas cities."]}, {"heading": "Why it matters now", "paragraphs": ["The listing is also a snapshot of how North Texas growth is changing the value proposition for large rural properties. Acreage that once felt remote can command a different premium when it remains within a reasonable drive of Dallas-Fort Worth, particularly when it already includes homes, barns, roads, water features and recreational improvements. Buyers at this end of the market may be evaluating conservation, cattle, hunting, equestrian use and long-term land appreciation at the same time. The Roosevelt connection makes the property memorable, but location and the difficulty of assembling 1,300 contiguous acres are likely to matter just as much to a serious buyer. As this story develops, readers should distinguish confirmed details from social-media speculation and watch the original reporting and official records for material updates. Keep TX Red will treat later changes as updates rather than silently folding unverified claims into the record."]}], "faq": [], "sources": [{"label": "Chron — source report", "url": "https://www.chron.com/texas/article/texas-ranch-fdr-grandson-21-5m-listing-22370871.php"}], "keyTakeaways": ["Rolling R Ranch in Cooke County combines family history, ranchland and luxury amenities just over an hour from Dallas."]}'::jsonb body_json,'/images/news/generated/2026-08-08-fdr-grandson-rolling-r-ranch-sale.svg'::text image_url,'FDR’s Grandson Lists 1,300-Acre North Texas Ranch for $21.5 Million editorial illustration'::text image_alt_text
